I didn't add the `http-client` import. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`, and the graph definition hasn't been updated yet. Adding the import would give this node authority its definition doesn't declare, and it would send item text to an external host. Building the URL by interpolating raw text into a query string would also need encoding that the spec doesn't cover. Once the graph lists `http-client` in the node's `with` clause, I can add it.

The crate below implements `RecordSeen` with the granted authority only. It marks each considered item id as seen in the `seen` store, keyed by id with the digest date as the value, and only when the digest was published. The spec doesn't say whether unpublished digests should mark items seen, so I assumed they shouldn't. If that's wrong, the change is one line.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;

        // Only a published digest marks its considered items as seen; an
        // unpublished one leaves them eligible for the next run.
        if published.published {
            for id in published.considered.iter() {
                // Ids are parser-computed digests; an empty one is not a valid key.
                if id.is_empty() {
                    continue;
                }
                state_rw::put(id, &published.date);
                recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
            }
        }

        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

